cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ConceptFlow in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ConceptFlow: Formal Concept Analysis for the scientific Python stack"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Anurag
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8292-3092"
    affiliation: University of Kassel
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/anuragxorma/conceptflow"
url: "https://conceptflow.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  ConceptFlow is a Python library for Formal Concept Analysis (FCA):
  formal contexts, concept lattices, implication bases, concept measures,
  conceptual scaling, Boolean and ordinal factorization, and lattice
  visualization, with scikit-learn compatible estimators.
keywords:
  - formal concept analysis
  - FCA
  - concept lattice
  - scikit-learn
  - implications
  - conceptual scaling
